<!-- Four Reasons Facebook Outperforms Other Ad Channels section -->
<section class="fb-outperform-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="fb-outperform-title">Four Reasons Facebook Outperforms Other <br>Ad Channels in the UAE</h2>
    <p class="fb-outperform-subtitle">Understanding what makes Facebook uniquely powerful for UAE market businesses:</p>
    <div class="row g-4">
      <!-- Card 1: Personalized content -->
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6">
        <div class="fb-outperform-card">
          <div class="fb-outperform-number">1</div>
          <h3 class="fb-outperform-card-title">Personalized content</h3>
          <p class="fb-outperform-card-desc">Google Ads targets intent- people already searching for something. Facebook targets identity- people based on who they are, what they care about, and how they behave online and offline. For brands that need to reach a very specific type of person in Dubai, a high-net-worth expat, a recently promoted manager, a parent of school-age children, or a business owner in a specific industry- Facebook's targeting depth makes campaigns possible that simply cannot be replicated anywhere else.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Card 2: Creative Formats for Stages of the Funnel -->
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6">
        <div class="fb-outperform-card">
          <div class="fb-outperform-number">2</div>
          <h3 class="fb-outperform-card-title">Creative Formats for Stages of the Funnel</h3>
          <p class="fb-outperform-card-desc">Facebook is not a text-based platform- it is a visual medium with an enormous variety of ad formats at your disposal. Video ads build awareness and emotion. Carousel ads showcase multiple products or features. Lead Ads capture contact information without friction. Dynamic Ads automatically serve personalized product recommendations to past website visitors. Each format serves a distinct purpose in the funnel, and BrandStory knows exactly when and how to deploy each one for maximum impact in the UAE market.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Card 3: The Power to Recover Lost Revenue -->
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6">
        <div class="fb-outperform-card">
          <div class="fb-outperform-number">3</div>
          <h3 class="fb-outperform-card-title">The Power to Recover Lost Revenue</h3>
          <p class="fb-outperform-card-desc">Studies consistently show that over 95% of website visitors leave without converting on their first visit. Facebook's Pixel-powered retargeting lets you follow those visitors across the Meta ecosystem - showing them highly relevant ads based on exactly what they looked at on your site, bringing them back when they are ready to make a decision. For e-commerce, real estate, automotive, and high-consideration service businesses in Dubai, this retargeting capability alone can dramatically increase revenue without increasing your acquisition cost.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Card 4: Platform That Scales With Business -->
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6">
        <div class="fb-outperform-card">
          <div class="fb-outperform-number">4</div>
          <h3 class="fb-outperform-card-title">Platform That Scales With Business</h3>
          <p class="fb-outperform-card-desc">Facebook Ads work at every stage of business growth. A startup in Dubai with AED 3,000 a month can generate meaningful leads. An established enterprise spending AED 50,000+ a month can build brand dominance across the entire GCC. Unlike many digital channels that hit a ceiling, Meta's platform has the audience size, targeting depth, and ad format variety to scale with your ambition - provided campaigns are built and managed by people who know what they are doing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<!-- How to Choose the Right Facebook Marketing Agency in Dubai section -->
<section class="brandstory-choose-us-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">How to Choose the Right Facebook Marketing Agency in Dubai</h2>
    <p class="section-subtitle">With dozens of agencies in Dubai claiming Facebook expertise, how do you know who to trust with your ad budget? Here are three questions every business should ask before signing with a Facebook marketing agency:</p>
    <div class="row g-4">
      <!-- Box 1: Do They Have UAE - Specific Experience? -->
      <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6">
        <div class="choose-card">
          <div class="choose-card-img-wrap">
            <img src="<?= base_url("assets/images/fb-image-05.webp") ?>" class="choose-card-img img-fluid" alt="Do They Have UAE - Specific Experience?">
          </div>
          <h3 class="choose-card-title">Do They Have UAE - Specific Experience?</h3>
          <p class="choose-card-desc">Running Facebook Ads in Dubai is fundamentally different from running them in Europe or the US. Audience behavior, cultural sensitivities, language preferences, peak usage times, and competitive CPMs all differ. An agency that has only worked in Western markets will apply strategies that simply do not fit. Ask for UAE-based campaign results - not generic global case studies.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Box 2: Will You Own Your Ad Account? -->
      <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6">
        <div class="choose-card">
          <div class="choose-card-img-wrap">
            <img src="<?= base_url("assets/images/fb-image-06.webp") ?>" class="choose-card-img img-fluid" alt="Will You Own Your Ad Account?">
          </div>
          <h3 class="choose-card-title">Will You Own Your Ad Account?</h3>
          <p class="choose-card-desc">Some agencies run your ads from their own agency account - meaning if you ever leave, you lose all your campaign history, audience data, and Pixel data. Always insist that campaigns run from an ad account owned by your business. BrandStory operates exclusively this way: your account, your data, your asset - we are the operator, not the owner.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Box 3: Is Creative Produced In - House? -->
      <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 mx-auto">
        <div class="choose-card">
          <div class="choose-card-img-wrap">
            <img src="<?= base_url("assets/images/fb-image-07.webp") ?>" class="choose-card-img img-fluid" alt="Is Creative Produced In - House?">
          </div>
          <h3 class="choose-card-title">Is Creative Produced In - House?</h3>
          <p class="choose-card-desc">Facebook's algorithm rewards high-quality, high-engagement creatives with lower CPMs and better delivery. Agencies that outsource creative work to freelancers or use generic stock-photo ads will consistently underperform. The creative and the strategy need to be built together by the same team - which is exactly how BrandStory operates.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
